abstract: "This dataset represents modeled areal extent of eelgrass meadows (Zostera\
  \ marina) in coastal British Columbia, Canada. This dataset was generated between\
  \ 2016 and 2017 as part of the Commission for Environmental Cooperation efforts\
  \ to estimate blue carbon storage in eelgrass meadows across the Pacific Northwest.\
  \  \nTo model the areal spatial extent of British Columbia a novel tool was created\
  \ for use in ArcGIS. This tool required 2 inputs: (1) the coastline data from Shorezone\
  \ (ie. vector line features with attributes on the presence or absence of eelgrass\
  \ along a linear extent of coastline) and (2) bathymetry data. Briefly, each line\
  \ segment of coast in ShoreZone was converted to points along its vertices and points\
  \ were used to generate Thiessen polygons. Thiessen polygons were clipped to a selected\
  \ bathymetric contour (5 m or 3 m) based on the results of regional bathymetry analysis.\
  \ The modeled outputs were compared to available mapping data from the British Columbia\
  \ Marine Conservation Analysis Atlas to assess model accuracy.  \nPlease refer to\
  \ the report summary for the details on methods and caveats. \n\nLimitations and\
  \ caveats:\n\nThe modeling outputs of this work were dependent on (1) the resolution\
  \ and accuracy of bathymetric data (which was not available for all parts of the\
  \ BC coast) and (2) ShoreZone coverage (not all parts of the BC coast were surveyed\
  \ using ShoreZone methods at the time of the analysis). ShoreZone data has been\
  \ shown to underestimate the presence of eelgrass and the ability of ShoreZone to\
  \ map the presence of eelgrass depends on eelgrass being visible in the intertidal\
  \ and shallow subtidal region during the low tide imagery acquisition, therefore\
  \ deeper subtidal beds are missed. ShoreZone data, and therefore these modeled outputs,\
  \ represents a snapshot in time. Given known long-term dynamics of eelgrass meadows,\
  \ these data do not indicate areas that have undergone losses or gains in eelgrass\
  \ extent.  \n\nPlease refer to the report summary which contains a map that shows\
  \ regions where eelgrass extent was not modeled due to the lack of available bathymetry\
  \ and/or ShoreZone data."
